FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1: give FA2 FP8 batch MLA modules their own JIT URI

Source: original to this port (no upstream source).
License: FlashInfer is Apache-2.0.
Upstream: not applicable (build-identity guard for the patched header).
Purpose: JIT module URIs encode only parameters (dtypes, head dims,
  profiler, plan ABI, _sm90), never source contents. get_aot_artifacts()
  serves a module from flashinfer/data/aot/ or from a jit-cache provider
  whose manifest lists the URI before any JIT build runs, and a JIT build
  directory is reused while ninja sees no newer input. A suffix on the FA2
  FP8 URI ensures the patched mla.cuh (0003) is what runs: no prebuilt
  artifact can match it, and a cache shared with an unpatched image
  cannot be reused. Optional for 0.7.0.post1, whose jit-cache has no FP8
  MLA module; keep it while 0003 is applied.

--- a/flashinfer/jit/attention/modules.py
+++ b/flashinfer/jit/attention/modules.py
@@ -223,7 +223,13 @@
         f"head_dim_ckv_{head_dim_ckv}_"
         f"head_dim_kpe_{head_dim_kpe}_"
         f"profiler_{use_profiler}_planabi2"
-    ) + ("_sm90" if backend == "fa3" else "")
+    ) + ("_sm90" if backend == "fa3" else "") + (
+        # Patched FP8 KV tile cap in mla.cuh: a distinct name so neither a
+        # jit-cache artifact nor an unpatched JIT build is ever reused.
+        "_fp8tilecap"
+        if backend == "fa2" and dtype_kv == torch.float8_e4m3fn
+        else ""
+    )
 
 
